# Console layout simplification plan

## Architecture

- `frontend/src/App.tsx` owns the shared console shell and nests the existing
  feed and entry-detail routes inside it. Its main header is the remaining
  product/console context after the sidebar is removed.
- `frontend/src/styles.css` defines the shell grid, main content spacing, and
  responsive layout. The sidebar selectors are isolated to the removed
  `<aside className="console-sidebar">` subtree.

## Issue dependency

- Issue #101 is self-contained and builds on the current console UI. It does
  not change API contracts, feed data, routing, or persistence.

## Design decisions

- Remove the sidebar DOM entirely rather than visually hiding it, eliminating
  unused navigation and preventing an empty accessibility landmark.
- Change `.console-shell` to one `minmax(0, 1fr)` column and delete the unused
  sidebar/product-mark/sidebar-note styles so no reserved gutter remains.
- Preserve `AppShell` as the route layout, keep `console-main` and its header
  unchanged, and retain the mobile rules that still apply to feed content.
- Validate with frontend typecheck, tests, production build, and a focused UI
  check that the feed occupies the full viewport width with the header intact.
